Z||000000||fierojp||12-23-2001||02:58 PM||||Hello,<BR>I have an '88 Coupe with a Quad 4.  Still trying to get a bunch of the little bugs worked out.  Right now I have the black wire with the white stripe that used to be connected to the 2.5L DIS (which goes to the tach) connected to the white wire coming from the Quad4 IDI (tach signal).  The reading on the tach seems high.  I don't have any kind of tach filter that I know of... don't think I need one either for this setup.  Anyone else have this same setup with a working tach??    <P>Thanks!<BR>J.P.||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierojp||12-23-2001||06:40 PM||||Nevermind on the tach.  It was just idling high for the first few seconds.  When I was driving, 3000RPM seemed to come almost immediately in first gear, but then again I've got the 3.94 gears in that Getrag!  <P>Now my oil pressure gauge shows 80+ anytime I turn the car on....  <P>JP||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||12-23-2001||07:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierojp:<BR><B>Now my oil pressure gauge shows 80+ anytime I turn the car on....  <P>JP</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It should.  My quad pegs the oil pressure gauge on startup.  After about 20 or so minutes of fairly normal highway driving it drops to about 40psi at 2,000 rpm.  If I drive it like I stole it, it's a little lower.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/quad_sig_pic_1.jpg">        <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierojp||12-23-2001||07:58 PM||||Thanks Standard!  Now that I think about it that makes sense too!  When I had the wrong computer in my car, it would heat up very fast since the timing was way off.  That would explain why it would only take 2 minutes for the oil pressure to begin dropping...  Thanks again!<P>JP||||reg||12
